  "content": {
    "id": "p52-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "$f(x)=x^2\\sin(-x)+x\\cos(-x)$. Decide whether $f(x)$ is odd, even, or neither.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Odd.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=-x^2\\sin x+x\\cos x\\\\f(-x)&=-(-x)^2\\sin(-x)+(-x)\\cos(-x)\\\\f(-x)&=x^2\\sin x-x\\cos x\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x)\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $f$ is odd.\n\nSketch this on Desmos, it looks really cool!",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
